    <item>
      <title>💗 Ever wondered why a remote Web3 job is only available in certain countries? Yo</title>
      <link>https://t.me/cryptojobslist/11674</link>
      <description>&lt;div class="tgme_widget_message_text js-message_text" dir="auto"&gt;&lt;tg-emoji emoji-id="5307620107931895779"&gt;&lt;i class="emoji" style="background-image:url('//telegram.org/img/emoji/40/F09F9297.png')"&gt;&lt;b&gt;💗&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/tg-emoji&gt; &lt;b&gt;Ever wondered why a remote Web3 job is only available in certain countries?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;You find a role that matches your experience, it's advertised as remote, but then you notice: &lt;i&gt;US only, EU residents, or specific time zones.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why does this happen?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;There are a few reasons companies might restrict where they hire:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;» &lt;b&gt;Legal and tax requirements:&lt;/b&gt; Hiring someone in another country can create additional employment, payroll and tax obligations.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;» &lt;b&gt;Time zone overlap:&lt;/b&gt; Some teams need people available during specific hours for meetings, customer support or collaboration.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;» &lt;b&gt;Employment arrangements:&lt;/b&gt; A company might only be set up to hire employees in certain countries, even if it works with international contractors.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;» &lt;b&gt;Work authorization:&lt;/b&gt; Certain positions require candidates to already have permission to work in a particular country.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;So even in an industry as globally connected as Web3, remote doesn't always mean worldwide.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;And being outside the eligible region doesn't necessarily mean you're unqualified for the role.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Next time you find an interesting opening, check the location and employment requirements before investing time in the application.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;tg-emoji emoji-id="5399818044866327279"&gt;&lt;i class="emoji" style="background-image:url('//telegram.org/img/emoji/40/F09F92AC.png')"&gt;&lt;b&gt;💬&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/tg-emoji&gt;&lt;b&gt; Have you ever found a great opportunity only to discover it wasn't available in your country?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://t.me/cryptojobslist/11674</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 07:35:56 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
